    'Tanzania is home to some of the greatest concentrations of wildlife on Earth and the continent\'s most iconic safari landscapes. The Serengeti — "endless plains" in the Maasai language — stretches across 14,750 km² of open savannah and forms the heart of the greatest wildlife migration on the planet. Each year over 1.5 million wildebeest and 200,000 zebras circle the Serengeti-Mara ecosystem in an endless search for grass and water.',
