  { q: 'What is the Great Migration and when is it in Tanzania?', a: 'The Great Migration is the continuous circular movement of over 1.5 million wildebeest around the Serengeti-Mara ecosystem. The herds are in Tanzania for approximately 9 months of the year. Calving season in the southern Serengeti peaks in February. The dramatic Grumeti River crossings occur in June and July. The herds move to Kenya from August to October before returning south.' },
